    "status": "draft",
    "summary": "Amends 006 sections 3.3 and 3.4. Every --json answer this product writes becomes the envelope spec-spine has written since 0.26.0 (its spec 132 section 3.4): schemaVersion, tool, verb, outcome, exitCode, summary, then report for exit 0 or 1 and error for 2, 3 or 4, where error.kind is one of the family's ten tokens. No exit number moves. A usage error under --json is an envelope on stdout. The replacement of 002 section 3.23's check translation, which #118 proposed for the same change, is left to the spec-spine 0.28.0 adoption, which changes the producer answer it would read. Replaces the section 5 proposal of #118, which the amendment model adopted on 2026-09-25 (001 section 5) no longer admits.\n",
    "title": "The family envelope: every --json answer in the exit and JSON contract spec-spine speaks"
  },
